_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_

**Refactor `GenerateStoryResult` to use a discriminated union for type safety.**

The non-null assertions on `storyId`, `storyFilePath`, and `exportedStoryName` are necessary because `GenerateStoryResult` uses `success: boolean` instead of a discriminated union with literal types. This prevents TypeScript from narrowing the optional fields within the `if (result.success)` block.



<details>
<summary>♻️ Recommended refactor</summary>

In `code/core/src/core-server/utils/generate-story.ts`, restructure `GenerateStoryResult` as a discriminated union:

```typescript
export type GenerateStoryResult =
  | {
      success: true;
      storyId: string;
      kind: string;
      storyFilePath: string;
      exportedStoryName: string;
    }
  | {
      success: false;
      kind?: string;
      storyFilePath?: string;
      error?: string;
      errorType?: 'STORY_FILE_EXISTS' | 'UNKNOWN';
    };
```

This allows TypeScript to automatically narrow types inside `if (result.success)` blocks, eliminating the need for non-null assertions at lines 34-36 and line 54.

</details>

